 "modules": [
  {
   "id": 1,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "CAMERA MOTION\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 1, CC 49 to 64\n   1 Frequency of angle changes\n   2 Hold\n   3 Camera carry\n   4 Camera move\n   5 Move speed\n   6 Move follows\n   7 Move starts on\n   8 Camera owner\n   9 Move against loudness\n  10 Shake\n  11 Time speed\n  12 Slow push in on a face\n  13 The camera circles them\n  14 Turning to reveal\n  15 The camera wanders off\n  16 The stretching background shot\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 1, CC 65 to 80\n   1 suite: Handheld hunt\n   2 suite: Smooth push\n   3 suite: Object insert\n   4 suite: Loving camera\n   5 suite: Aggressive camera\n   6 suite: Follows the voice\n   7 suite: Video game camera\n   8 suite: The floor drops\n   9 suite: Something in the room\n  10 pair: When the camera goes handheld, gesture grows\n  11 pair: When the player takes the camera, the view becomes theirs\n  12 pair: When a character crosses the room, the camera move starts with them\n  13 pair: When the camera follows a character, it tracks alongside them\n  14 pair: When the camera moves on a breath, a small pause opens up\n  15 pair: When the camera jumps on loud moments, the shot gets shakier\n  16 pair: When the camera turns to reveal a person, it becomes an entrance\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 1, CC 81 to 94\n   1 pair: When the camera pushes in on a face, we feel with them\n   2 pair: When the camera pushes in as they realise, the realisation lands\n   3 pair: When the background stretches, we feel it in the body\n   4 pair: When the sound drops out under the stretch, we hear through their ears\n   5 pair: When the camera circles a kiss, tenderness grows\n   6 pair: When the camera whirls around them, the feeling peaks\n   7 pair: When the turn reveals a threat, dread rises\n   8 pair: When the turn is a whip, the picture blurs\n   9 pair: When the camera wanders off to a clue, the audience holds a question\n  10 pair: When the camera wanders off, it lingers where it lands\n  11 pairs: The camera answers the body\n  12 pairs: Camera moves with a reason\n  13 pairs: The ground gives way\n  14 pairs: Someone is there"
   },
   "pos": [
